## What this does not cover

**Software** — `src/`, `pipeline/demark/`, `tests/` — is MIT. See `LICENSE`.

**Corpus specimens and their derived variants** under `corpus/` are derived from
the Astro documentation (github.com/withastro/docs), which is MIT licensed. That
license travels with the material and with anything derived from it. This
repository does not, and cannot, relicense it. See `corpus/NOTICE`.

This matters for `artifacts/` too: pipeline artifacts contain rendered and
extracted corpus text, so to the extent an artifact reproduces Astro's content it
carries Astro's terms. The CC BY grant above applies to the study's own
contribution — the selection, the transformation, the coding, and the analysis —
not to the underlying documentation.

The implicit-arm variants are **derivative works created by this study**. They are
mechanically degraded on purpose and are not Astro's documentation. Anyone
redistributing them should say so, in addition to preserving Astro's attribution.
